Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:45:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 092/154] fix(window): read settings.json off the UI thread
 when a window opens
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The constructor read the file inline. Only the first profile's window is built
before BrowserMainLoop disallows blocking, so every later one aborted. The
read moves to a thread-pool runner behind a process-wide cache, and the reply
fills the cache and mirrors this profile's engines as before.

The cache holds one copy for the process and serves every window from it, so a
second window pays for no second read.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 91ea480f28974..06b72718a0504 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -652,6 +652,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:pinch_gesture_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:restore_plan",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:search_engine_mirror",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:settings_json_cache",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:sidebar_drop_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:sidebar_grip_bounds",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:sidebar_move_execution_decision",
